    "reply": "The catalogued findings delineate numerous sequence alterations mapped to the NM_000492.4 transcript of CFTR across diverse protein domains [1]. Additional catalogued entries are archived as dedicated database records without explicit nomenclature strings [10]. \n\n## Amino Terminal Variants\n\nAn early alteration is designated as NM_000492.4(CFTR):c.242T>A (p.Phe81Tyr) [20]. Another amino-terminal alteration is catalogued as NM_000492.4(CFTR):c.364T>A (p.Tyr122Asn) [12]. Nearby changes include NM_000492.4(CFTR):c.389T>C (p.Leu130Pro) [17]. A adjacent residue variant is NM_000492.4(CFTR):c.407T>G (p.Leu136Arg) [18].\n\n## Central Coding Variants\n\nWithin central coding regions, one characterized alteration is NM_000492.4(CFTR):c.1051A>G (p.Thr351Ala) [5]. A synonymous alteration is identified as NM_000492.4(CFTR):c.1077A>G (p.Gln359=) [27]. Another central missense event is NM_000492.4(CFTR):c.1384G>A (p.Ala462Thr) [1]. A further substitution is NM_000492.4(CFTR):c.1444A>G (p.Ile482Val) [25].\n\n## Carboxy Terminal Variants\n\nMore distal alterations include NM_000492.4(CFTR):c.3691T>C (p.Ser1231Pro) [8]. Another downstream event is NM_000492.4(CFTR):c.3767C>G (p.Ala1256Gly) [30]. Toward the terminus lies NM_000492.4(CFTR):c.4028G>A (p.Gly1343Asp) [13]. The most distal variant is NM_000492.4(CFTR):c.4244T>G (p.Val1415Gly) [14].\n\n## Unannotated Accession Records\n\nSeveral findings represent sequence variant records defined by identifiers, including SequenceVariant record ClinVar:1012571 [10]. Another entry is SequenceVariant record ClinVar:1012572 [11]. Further entries include SequenceVariant record ClinVar:1027585 [15]. A corresponding listing is SequenceVariant record ClinVar:1027591 [16].",
